WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:01.210
The nearest stars.

00:01.856 --> 00:04.085
The Sun is one star among its neighbours.

00:04.480 --> 00:13.135
The nearest, Proxima Centauri, is 4.2 light-years away, and its two companions are the nearest stars you can see without a telescope.

00:13.799 --> 00:16.624
Each point here is a star at its measured distance.
